<p>Use the following procedure to have text stamped on prints. </p>
<p>To create, edit, and delete a watermark, see the following procedures:</p>
<p><a href="~/Topics/IDH_HOW_WATERMARK#print">Printing a Watermark</a></p>
<p><a href="~/Topics/IDH_HOW_WATERMARK#create">Editing a Watermark/Creating 
 a New Watermark</a></p>
<p><a href="~/Topics/IDH_HOW_WATERMARK#delete">Deleting a Watermark</a></p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>You cannot update or delete system-provided watermarks.</p></li>
</ul>
<h2>Printing a Watermark</h2>
<ol>
<li><p>Open the printing preferences dialog box after 
 creating a document in an application.</p></li>
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">Effects</span> 
 menu on the <span class="Term-Soft">Detailed Settings</span> tab.</p></li>
<li><p>Select the <span class="Term-Soft">Print Watermark</span> 
 check box. </p></li>
<li><p>Select a watermark in the <span class="Term-Soft">Watermarks:</span> 
 list.</p></li>
</ol>
<div class="help-step-extra">
<ul>
<li><p class="Normal-indent">To see the 
 details of the watermark, click <span class="Term-Soft">Edit</span>.</p></li>
</ul>
</div>
<ol start="5">
<li><p>After making any other necessary settings, click 
 <span class="Term-OS">OK</span> to close the printing preferences dialog 
 box.</p></li>
<li><p>Start printing.</p></li>
</ol>
<h2>Editing a Watermark/Creating a New Watermark</h2>
<ol>
<li><p>Open the printing preferences dialog box.</p></li>
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">Effects</span> 
 menu on the <span class="Term-Soft">Detailed Settings</span> tab.</p></li>
<li><p>Select the <span class="Term-Soft">Print Watermark</span> 
 check box. Click <span class="Term-Soft">Edit...</span> to open a dialog 
 box.</p></li>
<li><p>In the <span class="Term-Soft">Watermarks:</span> 
 list, select the watermark that you want to edit.<br/>
 If you want to register a new watermark, enter a name for it in the 
 <span class="Term-Soft">Name:</span> box.</p></li>
<li><p>Enter the text in the <span class="Term-Soft">Text:</span> 
 box. The text appears in the preview window.</p></li>
<li><p>To change the font, font style and color, specify 
 from the <span class="Term-Soft">Font:</span>, <span class="Term-Soft">Font 
 Style:</span>, <span class="Term-Soft">Color:</span>, and <span class="Term-Soft">Frame/Outline:</span> 
 lists.</p></li>
</ol>
<ol start="7">
<li><p>To change the text size, angle, and density, specify 
 a value in the <span class="Term-Soft">Size:</span>, <span class="Term-Soft">Angle:</span>, 
 and <span class="Term-Soft">Density:</span> boxes.</p></li>
<li><p>Select a printing position where you want to print 
 a watermark in the <span class="Term-Soft">Position:</span> list.</p></li>
<li><p>To print the watermark on the first page only, 
 select the <span class="Term-Soft">First Page Only</span> check box.</p></li>
<li><p>To place the watermark over the image, select 
 the <span class="Term-Soft">Opaque</span> check box. The image under the 
 watermark will not be visible.</p></li>
<li><p>To print the watermark repeatedly, select the 
 <span class="Term-Soft">Repeat</span> check box.</p></li>
<li><p>To print the watermark on each original page when 
 <span class="Term-Soft">Layout</span> or <span class="Term-Soft">Booklet</span> 
 setting is applied, select the <span class="Term-Soft">Per Original Page 
 </span>check box.</p></li>
<li><p>After specifying the settings, click<span class="Term-Soft"> 
 Add</span> or <span class="Term-Soft">Update</span> to save the watermark.<br/>
 If you click <span class="Term-Soft">Update</span>, a dialog box appears 
 asking if you want to overwrite the old watermark. Click <span class="Term-Soft">Yes</span>.</p></li>
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-Soft">OK</span> to close 
 the dialog box.</p></li>
</ol>
<h2>Deleting a Watermark</h2>
<ol>
<li><p>Open the printing preferences dialog box.</p></li>
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">Effects</span> 
 menu on the <span class="Term-Soft">Detailed Settings</span> tab.</p></li>
<li><p>Select the <span class="Term-Soft">Print Watermark</span> 
 check box. Click <span class="Term-Soft">Edit...</span> to open a dialog 
 box.</p></li>
<li><p>Select a watermark from the <span class="Term-Soft">Watermarks:</span> 
 list, and then click <span class="Term-Soft">Delete</span>. </p></li>
<li><p>A dialog box appears prompting for confirmation. 
 Click <span class="Term-Soft">Yes</span>.</p></li>
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-Soft">OK</span> to close 
 the dialog box.</p></li>
</ol>
